                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "The top-rated car rental companies in London and Paris are Green Motion and Paris Rent-a-Car, respectively. The most expensive restaurants in London are House of Sushi and Home Kitchen, while in Paris, they are Breizh Caf\u00e9 and Bistrot Paul Bert. The most expensive hotels in London and Paris are Riverside View and Luxury Palace, respectively.\n\nThe total maximum expense for the 5-day trip, assuming 2 meals per day, would be:\n\n* Car rental: 59.0 euros/day (Green Motion) + 45.0 euros/day (Paris Rent-a-Car) = 104.0 euros/day\n* Food: 40.0 euros/meal (House of Sushi) + 35.0 euros/meal (Home Kitchen) = 75.0 euros/meal (London)\n* Food: 60.0 euros/meal (Breizh Caf\u00e9) + 40.0 euros/meal (Bistrot Paul Bert) = 100.0 euros/meal (Paris)\n* Hotel: 350.0 euros/night (Riverside View) + 1000.0 euros/night (Luxury Palace) = 1350.0 euros/night\n\nTotal maximum expense for the 5-day trip: 104.0 euros/day (car rental) + 75.0 euros/meal x 2 meals/day x 2 days (London) + 100.0 euros/meal x 2 meals/day x 3 days (Paris) + 1350.0 euros/night x 2 nights (London) + 1350.0 euros/night x 3 nights (Paris) = 104.0 euros/day x 5 days + 150.0 euros/day x 2 days + 200.0 euros/day x 3 days + 2700.0 euros + 4050.0 euros = 520.0 euros + 300.0 euros + 600.0 euros + 2700.0 euros + 4050.0 euros = 8170.0 euros\n\nNote: The prices are in euros and are based on the provided information. The actual prices may vary depending on various factors such as season, availability, and other factors."
